# 2. CIFAR From Scratch: Paper-Style LR

This section keeps the previous/paper-inspired learning rate:

```text
LR = 0.001
```

Purpose:

- reproduce the previous behavior
- keep a conservative/stable configuration
- compare communication methods without changing too many training variables

Dataset:

```yaml
data.dataset: "cifar10"
data.input_size: 32
data.augmentation:
  pad: 4
  random_crop: 32
  hflip: 0.5
data.normalize: "cifar10"
```

## 2.1 WideResNet50-2 on CIFAR

Why:

- larger than standard ResNet-50
- useful for stressing computation and communication
- still simpler than ResNeXt101-32x8d

Configuration:

```yaml
model.name: "wide_resnet50_2"
model.stem: "cifar"
model.norm: "batchnorm"
model.pretrained: false
model.num_classes: 10

train.batch_mode: "strong"   # or "weak"
train.global_batch_size: 256 # for strong scaling
train.local_batch_size: 128  # for weak scaling

opt.name: "sgd"
opt.lr: 0.001
opt.momentum: 0.9
opt.weight_decay: 1e-4

# Not specified in the paper:
sched.name: null
precision.mode: null

#usually better hypotesis: 
#sched.name: "cosine"
#sched.epochs: 200
#sched.warmup_epochs: 0
#precision.mode: "fp32"
```

## 2.2 ResNeXt101-32x8d on CIFAR

Why:

- much heavier model
- stronger communication/computation workload
- useful to test whether the proposed method helps more on larger models

Configuration:

```yaml
model.name: "resnext101_32x8d"
model.stem: "cifar"
model.norm: "batchnorm"
model.pretrained: false
model.num_classes: 10

train.batch_mode: "strong"   # or "weak"
train.global_batch_size: 256 # for strong scaling
train.local_batch_size: 128  # for weak scaling

opt.name: "sgd"
opt.lr: 0.001
opt.momentum: 0.9
opt.weight_decay: 1e-4

# Not specified in the paper:
sched.name: null
precision.mode: null

#usually better hypotesis: 
#sched.name: "cosine"
#sched.epochs: 200
#sched.warmup_epochs: 0
#precision.mode: "fp32"
```

Notes:

- `LR = 0.001` is conservative.
- This is useful for reproducing the previous setup, but may be too low for good CIFAR accuracy from scratch.
- If accuracy is poor or training is too slow, use Section 3.

