# 4. ImageNet / ImageNet-Like Experiments

Purpose:

- test the same models on larger, more realistic inputs
- evaluate communication behavior with heavier compute
- optionally use pretrained models for faster correctness checks

Dataset:

```yaml
data.dataset: "imagenet_like"
data.input_size: 224
data.augmentation:
  random_resized_crop: 224
  hflip: 0.5
data.validation:
  resize: 256
  center_crop: 224
```

Use ImageNet stem:

```yaml
model.stem: "imagenet"
```

This means:

```text
7x7 conv, stride 2
maxpool
```

## 4.1 WideResNet50-2 ImageNet-Style Config

### From Scratch

```yaml
model.name: "wide_resnet50_2"
model.stem: "imagenet"
model.norm: "batchnorm"
model.pretrained: false
model.num_classes: <num_classes>

train.batch_mode: "strong"
train.global_batch_size: 256

opt.name: "sgd"
opt.lr: 0.1
opt.momentum: 0.9
opt.weight_decay: 1e-4
opt.lr_scaling: "linear_with_global_batch"

sched.name: "cosine"
sched.epochs: 90
sched.warmup_epochs: 5

precision.mode: "amp_fp16"
```

### Pretrained Fine-Tuning

```yaml
model.name: "wide_resnet50_2"
model.stem: "imagenet"
model.norm: "batchnorm"
model.pretrained: true
model.num_classes: <num_classes>

train.batch_mode: "strong"
train.global_batch_size: 256

opt.name: "sgd"
opt.lr: 0.001
opt.momentum: 0.9
opt.weight_decay: 1e-4

sched.name: "cosine"
sched.epochs: 5-20
sched.warmup_epochs: 0-1

precision.mode: "amp_fp16"
```

## 4.2 ResNeXt101-32x8d ImageNet-Style Config

Use an NVIDIA-style ImageNet recipe, adapted from ResNeXt101-32x4d to ResNeXt101-32x8d.

Important:

- NVIDIA’s public example is for `resnext101_32x4d`.
- This project uses `resnext101_32x8d`.
- `32x8d` is wider/heavier, so timing and memory use will differ.
- The recipe style is still useful: ImageNet stem, SGD, cosine LR, warmup, label smoothing, AMP.

### From Scratch

```yaml
model.name: "resnext101_32x8d"
model.stem: "imagenet"
model.norm: "batchnorm"
model.pretrained: false
model.num_classes: <num_classes>

train.batch_mode: "strong"
train.global_batch_size: 256
train.label_smoothing: 0.1

opt.name: "sgd"
opt.lr: 0.1
opt.momentum: 0.9
opt.weight_decay: 1e-4
opt.lr_scaling: "linear_with_global_batch"

sched.name: "cosine"
sched.epochs: 90
sched.warmup_epochs: 5

precision.mode: "amp_fp16"
```

Alternative closer to NVIDIA ResNeXt101-32x4d recipe:

```yaml
opt.lr: 0.256
opt.momentum: 0.875
opt.weight_decay: 6.103515625e-05
opt.apply_weight_decay_to_bn: false
train.label_smoothing: 0.1
```

Recommended approach:

- start with `lr = 0.1`, `momentum = 0.9`, `weight_decay = 1e-4`
- use the NVIDIA-style alternative only as a separate recipe variant
- do not mix recipe variants inside the same comparison table

### Pretrained Fine-Tuning

```yaml
model.name: "resnext101_32x8d"
model.stem: "imagenet"
model.norm: "batchnorm"
model.pretrained: true
model.num_classes: <num_classes>

train.batch_mode: "strong"
train.global_batch_size: 256

opt.name: "sgd"
opt.lr: 0.001
opt.momentum: 0.9
opt.weight_decay: 1e-4

sched.name: "cosine"
sched.epochs: 5-20
sched.warmup_epochs: 0-1

precision.mode: "amp_fp16"
```

